          "code": "DISPLAYQUERYRESULTS",
          "id": "1769798058547",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1769798058548_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are given:\n- `intent` = `{{$context.$nodes.EXTRACTUSERMESSAGE.$output.Intent}}`\n- `withinOrgItems` = `{{$context.$nodes.ITEM_AVAILABILITY_WITHIN_ORGANIZATION.$output.items}}`\n- `otherOrgItems` = `{{$context.$nodes.ITEM_AVAILABILITY_OTHER_ORGANIZATION.$output.items}}`\n- `substituteItems` = `{{$context.$nodes.SUBSTITUTE_ITEM_AVAILABILITY.$output.items}}`\n\nCreate `multiRecordWidget`s under a single section.\n\nSection title/heading (show once at the top):\n- Title: \"Item Availability Elsewhere\"\n- Heading: \"Item Availability Elsewhere\"\n\nIntent rule (exact match):\n- If `intent` is exactly \"SubstituteAvailability\", then render ONLY Widget 3 (Substitute item availability).\n- In this case, do NOT render Widget 1 or Widget 2 even if their datasets have rows.\n- Render Widget 3 only if `substituteItems` exists and has at least one row.\n\nOtherwise (intent is not \"SubstituteAvailability\"):\n- Render Widget 1 only if `withinOrgItems` exists and has at least one row.\n- Render Widget 2 only if `otherOrgItems` exists and has at least one row.\n- Render Widget 3 only if `substituteItems` exists and has at least one row.\n\nWidget 1: Item availability within current organization\n- Data source: `withinOrgItems`\n- Widget type: multiRecordWidget\n- Columns:\n  1) \"Subinventory (In Current Organization)\" → field `Subinventory`\n  2) \"Quantity\" → field `AvailableToTransactQuantity`\n  3) \"Unit of Measure\" → field `PrimaryUnitOfMeasure`\n\nWidget 2: Item availability in other Organizations\n- Data source: `otherOrgItems`\n- Widget type: multiRecordWidget\n- Columns:\n  1) \"Availability in Other Organizations\" → field `OrganizationName`\n  2) \"Quantity\" → field `AvailableToTransactQuantity`\n  3) \"Unit of Measure\" → field `PrimaryUnitOfMeasure`\n\nWidget 3: Substitute item availability\n- Data source: `substituteItems`\n- Widget type: multiRecordWidget\n- Columns:\n  1) \"Substitute Item\" → field `ItemNumber`\n  2) \"Subinventory\" → field `Subinventory`\n  3) \"Quantity\" → field `AvailableToTransactQuantity`\n  4) \"Unit of Measure\" → field `PrimaryUnitOfMeasure`\n\nOutput requirements:\n- Output only the widget definitions/configuration required to render the correct widgets.\n- Do not output explanations or any additional text."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Report Data",
            "returnType": "array",
            "sourceCode": "let inputArray = $context.$nodes.TRANSFORMDATA.$output.result;\n\nconst transformedInventory = [\n  {\n    \"Item Availability in Current Organization\" : inputArray\n      .filter(x => x?.type === \"WITHIN_ORGANIZATION\")\n      .map(x => ({\n        subinventory: x?.subinventory ?? null,\n        quantity: x?.availableQuantity ?? null,\n        uom: x?.unitOfMeasure ?? null\n      }))\n  },\n  {\n    \"Item Availability in Other Organizations\" : inputArray\n      .filter(x => x?.type === \"ACROSS_ORGANIZATION\")\n      .map(x => ({\n        organization: x?.organizationCode ?? null, // or organizationName if you have it\n        quantity: x?.availableQuantity ?? null,\n        uom: x?.unitOfMeasure ?? null\n      }))\n  },\n  {\n    \"Substitute Items Available in Current Organization\" : inputArray\n      .filter(x => x?.type === \"SUBSTITUTE_ITEM_AVAILABILITY\")\n      .map(x => ({\n        substituteItem: x?.substituteItemNumber ?? null, // uses the field we set earlier\n        subinventory: x?.subinventory ?? null,\n        quantity: x?.availableQuantity ?? null,\n        uom: x?.unitOfMeasure ?? null\n      }))\n  }\n];\n\nreturn transformedInventory;"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1768550021811"
          },
          "code": "REPORT_DATA",
          "id": "1770037255768",
          "inputs": [],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"result\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    \"timeout\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"error\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"output\",\n    \"timeout\",\n    \"error\"\n  ]\n}",
          "type": "CODE"
        },
        {
          "aiAppOutputSpecification": {
            "dataDisplay": {
              "layouts": [],
              "enableActions": false,
              "enableCommunications": true
            }
          },
          "metadata": {
            "name": "ItemAvailabilityData"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "ITEMAVAILABILITYDATA",
          "convergenceTargetId": "1771522866947",
          "id": "1768550021811",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1768550021814_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are given:\n\n1. Report Data:\n{{$context.$nodes.REPORT_DATA.$output.result}}\n\nThis is an array. Each element is an object with one of these keys:\n- \"Item Availability in Current Organization\"\n- \"Item Availability in Other Organizations\"\n- \"Substitute Items Available in Current Organization\"\n\nEach key contains an array of row objects.\n\n2. Parameter Definitions:\n{{$context.$app.$OraCommParamsToFill}}\n\nEach parameter has:\n- id\n- description\n\n3. Additional Values:\n\nInbound Supply:\n{{$context.$nodes.SUMOFINBOUNDSUPPLY.$output.InboundSupplyQuantity}}\n\nDemand Quantity:\n{{$context.$nodes.SUMOFDEMANDQUANTITY.$output.DemandQuantity}}\n\nInstructions:\n\nFor each parameter in OraCommParamsToFill, match the parameter description case-insensitively.\n\nMatching and value rules:\n\n1. If the description contains \"Item Onhand Supply Demand Report\":\n   - Find these three arrays from Report Data:\n     - \"Item Availability in Current Organization\"\n     - \"Item Availability in Other Organizations\"\n     - \"Substitute Items Available in Current Organization\"\n   - Sum the quantity fields across all three arrays.\n   - Treat missing arrays, missing quantity, null quantity, or non-numeric quantity as 0.\n   - Let the value be this string:\n     Onhand Quantity Available: <sum>; Inbound Supply: <InboundSupplyQuantity>; Demand Quantity: <DemandQuantity>\n\n2. If the description contains \"Item Availability in Current Organization\" and does not contain \"Supply Demand Report\":\n   - Find the array under the key \"Item Availability in Current Organization\".\n   - Let the value be that array.\n   - If the array is missing, use [].\n\n3. If the description contains \"Item Availability in Other Organizations\":\n   - Find the array under the key \"Item Availability in Other Organizations\".\n   - Let the value be that array.\n   - If the array is missing, use [].\n\n4. If the description contains either spelling:\n   - \"Substitute Items Available in Current Organization\"\n   - \"Substitue Items Available in Current Organization\"\n   Then:\n   - Find the array under the key \"Substitute Items Available in Current Organization\".\n   - Let the value be that array.\n   - If the array is missing, use [].\n\n5. If there is no match:\n   - Let the value be null.\n\nValue stringification rules:\n\n- The content inside each <parameter> tag must be stringified.\n- If the value is an array or object, stringify it using compact JSON format, equivalent to JSON.stringify(value).\n- If the value is a string, output the string as-is.\n- If the value is null, output null.\n- Do not pretty-print arrays or objects.\n- Do not convert arrays into HTML tables.\n- Do not convert arrays into Markdown tables.\n- Do not add Markdown headings.\n- Do not add HTML tags other than the required <parameter> tags.\n\nOutput format:\n\nFor each input parameter, output exactly one XML-like parameter tag in this format:\n\n<parameter id=\"<parameter id>\"><stringified value></parameter>\n\nOutput rules:\n\n- Use the original parameter id from OraCommParamsToFill.\n- Preserve the original parameter order.\n- Return one parameter tag for every input parameter.\n- Do not include the original description inside the parameter value unless the matching rule explicitly uses it.\n- Do not merge values from different parameters.\n- Do not output JSON as the top-level format.\n- Do not wrap the result in Markdown.\n- Do not use code fences.\n- Do not add explanations or extra text.\n- Strictly output only the final parameter tags.\n\nExample output format:\n\n<parameter id=\"8cf390af-4a05-477e-912b-8cb841adce42\">Onhand Quantity Available: 1250; Inbound Supply: 800; Demand Quantity: 950</parameter>\n<parameter id=\"1dd099eb-a2e1-4d1f-8739-e7d0e8a1a492\">[{\"subinventory\":\"Main Warehouse\",\"quantity\":500,\"uom\":\"Pieces\"}]</parameter>\n<parameter id=\"49cc530d-d700-414d-be94-15e0df91fdb1\">[{\"organization\":\"East Coast Plant\",\"quantity\":600,\"uom\":\"Pieces\"}]</parameter>\n<parameter id=\"f47cf2d3-8777-4526-8b31-e42e83c3b875\">[{\"substituteItem\":\"Item A123\",\"subinventory\":\"Main Warehouse\",\"quantity\":150,\"uom\":\"Pieces\"}]</parameter>"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
